{"id":"g.math.inequalities.3.e618f0bb4f","section":"math","domain":"algebra","skill":"inequalities","difficulty":3,"prompt":"A tutor earns $\\$50$ per hour for in-person sessions and $\\$32$ per hour for online sessions. This week she wants to earn at least $\\$900$ while working no more than 28 hours in total. If she works 12 hours in person, what is the minimum whole number of online hours she must work?","answer":["10"],"explanation":"In-person earnings: $12 \\times 50 = 600$. She needs $600 + 32h \\ge 900$, so $h \\ge 9.38$. The minimum whole number is $10$, and $12 + 10 \\le 28$ keeps her within the hour limit."},
{"id":"g.math.inequalities.3.197a286ec3","section":"math","domain":"algebra","skill":"inequalities","difficulty":3,"prompt":"A tutor earns $\\$40$ per hour for in-person sessions and $\\$25$ per hour for online sessions. This week she wants to earn at least $\\$850$ while working no more than 34 hours in total. If she works 8 hours in person, what is the minimum whole number of online hours she must work?","answer":["22"],"explanation":"In-person earnings: $8 \\times 40 = 320$. She needs $320 + 25h \\ge 850$, so $h \\ge 21.2$. The minimum whole number is $22$, and $8 + 22 \\le 34$ keeps her within the hour limit."},
{"id":"g.math.inequalities.3.7ab5e69175","section":"math","domain":"algebra","skill":"inequalities","difficulty":3,"prompt":"A tutor earns $\\$45$ per hour for in-person sessions and $\\$30$ per hour for online sessions. This week she wants to earn at least $\\$1{,}200$ while working no more than 34 hours in total. If she works 15 hours in person, what is the minimum whole number of online hours she must work?","answer":["18"],"explanation":"In-person earnings: $15 \\times 45 = 675$. She needs $675 + 30h \\ge 1200$, so $h \\ge 17.5$. The minimum whole number is $18$, and $15 + 18 \\le 34$ keeps her within the hour limit."},
{"id":"g.math.inequalities.3.97a2bfde11","section":"math","domain":"algebra","skill":"inequalities","difficulty":3,"prompt":"A tutor earns $\\$40$ per hour for in-person sessions and $\\$25$ per hour for online sessions. This week she wants to earn at least $\\$850$ while working no more than 25 hours in total. If she works 17 hours in person, what is the minimum whole number of online hours she must work?","answer":["7"],"explanation":"In-person earnings: $17 \\times 40 = 680$. She needs $680 + 25h \\ge 850$, so $h \\ge 6.8$. The minimum whole number is $7$, and $17 + 7 \\le 25$ keeps her within the hour limit."}
